WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.376
When you speak, a muscle lifts the soft palate against the back of the throat.

00:00:04.726 --> 00:00:06.369
This closes off the nose.

00:00:07.169 --> 00:00:10.881
After a cleft palate repair, the soft palate can be too short to reach.

00:00:11.231 --> 00:00:13.919
Air leaks into the nose, and speech sounds nasal.

00:00:14.719 --> 00:00:17.449
Practice cannot close this gap. It needs surgery.

00:00:18.249 --> 00:00:21.641
Here, a strip of tissue from the throat is joined to the soft palate.

00:00:22.441 --> 00:00:25.552
A speech pathologist checks speech before and after surgery,

00:00:25.552 --> 00:00:27.625
and treats sounds learned the wrong way.
